laurel 2100: XNU gets 3264 MiB of the 6 GB Mi A3 (was 768 MiB). Memory map: 0x80000000-0xE0000000 device pools outside kernel RAM (Adreno GPU pool 0xC0000000 + 512 MiB, room below it), 0xE0000000-0xE1000000 TopazModem pool (16 MiB), 0xE1000000-0x1C0000000 Mu 'Kernel RAM' with the DarwinBoot window 0xE1004000..0x1AD004000 (DDR banks B and C touch; UEFI allocates top-down from 0x1C0000000 above it). Self-check before arm_vm_init (osfmk/arm64/laurel_ram.c): the window must lie inside one run of the ADT /chosen laurel-ram-banks, at most 4608 MiB (TOPAZ_4K BOOTSTRAP_TABLE_SIZE), and overlap no /chosen laurel-ram-reserved pool (a pool above the base caps it); else (or laurelram=0) XNU keeps the first 768 MiB as before. A window of 768 MiB or less (old ADT/Mu FD) is left alone. USB and UFS DMA blocks (kmem_alloc_contig) now stay below 4 GiB. One line at EARLY_BOOT, again at the first surface: 'LAUREL RAM: on: 3264 MiB at 0xe1004000..0x1ad004000 (banks 0x80000000..0x1c0000000; 495 MiB below 4 GiB)' or 'LAUREL RAM: off: <reason>; XNU keeps 768 MiB ...'. Needs patches/laurel/mu/0101 and mkadt.py --dram auto.

